## What G3CO left open

G3CO proves that the complete original-Jacobian map in Cox degree
`(9,1,3)` is surjective at every point of the selected path with

```text
0<t<=1.
```

It deliberately does not claim the same unsaturated presentation theorem at
the algebraic start `t=0`, `a=1`. That is a real algebraic distinction, but it
is not a possible singularity of the geometric transport.

## Smooth proper start

G3BI proves that `a=1` is a smooth characteristic-zero complete intersection.
G3BJ embeds it in a smooth proper one-parameter family and supplies the
rank-1,509 Gauss-Manin local system. Hence, on a neighborhood `U` of `a=1`,
relative de Rham cohomology is a finite locally free bundle

```text
H = R^n f_* Omega^bullet_(X/U)
```

with regular Gauss-Manin connection

```text
nabla_GM : H -> H tensor Omega^1_U.
```

G3CL independently proves that the fixed augmented B103/Macaulay frame is a
regular 1,510-dimensional frame at `a=1`. In that frame,

```text
Omega_std = E_std^-1 nabla_GM E_std
```

belongs to `Mat_1510(O_U)`. In particular, `Omega_std(1)` exists and is finite.

## Why a pole-six pole must cancel

On the punctured selected path, G3CO supplies an exact rational
original-Jacobian right inverse in degree `(9,1,3)`. Compose it with exact
Griffiths-Dwork divergence and the regular lower Hodge parent charts. The
result represents the same Gauss-Manin connection as `Omega_std` wherever
both constructions are defined.

That common domain contains infinitely many points accumulating at `a=1`.
The two meromorphic matrices therefore agree identically there. Since
`Omega_std` is regular at `a=1`, every apparent pole in the complete rational
reduction is removable. A failure of the raw unsaturated Jacobian map at the
single start fiber could only mean that this particular coefficient
presentation degenerates; it cannot make the Gauss-Manin transport singular.

Thus the full `208570 x 602597` start-rank calculation is optional for
transport existence. It remains useful only if one wants that exact raw
Jacobian gauge at `a=1`.

## Initial-value consequence

For

```text
a(t)=1-t+i*pi*t*(1-t),
a'(t)=-1+i*pi*(1-2t),
```

the standard-frame equation is

```text
Y_dot=A(t)Y,
A(t)=a'(t) Omega_std(a(t)).
```

The coefficient `A(t)` is continuous at `t=0`. The selected geometric source
`z4=-delta tensor u_B` therefore has a unique local continuation once its
standard-frame embedding is supplied. If a certified ball gives

```text
sup_(0<=t<=epsilon) ||A(t)|| <= L,
```

then the omitted start segment obeys the explicit enclosure

```text
||Y(epsilon)-Y(0)||
  <= (exp(L*epsilon)-1) ||Y(0)||.
```

This gives a rigorous alternative to evaluating the raw start inverse.

